# ADR-001: this file does NOT control embedding (that is the reactor's
# maven-dependency-plugin `embed-dependencies` execution, includeScope=runtime,
# excludeTransitive=true - see docs/ADR/001-embed-third-party-dependencies.md).
# It exists solely to correct bnd's automatically generated Import-Package
# for the OSGi manifest.
#
# netty-codec-compression (embedded transitively via netty-codec-http, needed
# for the WebSocket handshake) contains encoder/decoder classes for several
# OPTIONAL compression backends (Brotli, Zstd, LZ4, LZMA, JZlib/zlib, LZF).
# None of these backend libraries are embedded (see pom.xml) because this
# binding never uses HTTP content-encoding - SHIP is a raw WebSocket/TLS
# protocol. Without this override, bnd's static bytecode analysis treats
# every one of these as a MANDATORY Import-Package, and karaf-feature-verification
# fails one missing package at a time (already seen for
# com.aayushatharva.brotli4j). Marking them resolution:=optional keeps them
# out of the way of feature verification while still declaring the
# capability accurately, should the backing library ever actually be
# installed at runtime.
# com.oracle.svm.* / org.graalvm.*: GraalVM native-image (Substrate VM) support
# annotations and SDK types (@TargetClass/@Substitute-style classes, polyglot
# API), present for optional native-image compatibility in one or more of the
# embedded JAXB/Jackson/Netty-ecosystem jars (angus-activation declares an
# optional/provided dependency on org.graalvm.sdk:graal-sdk, for example).
# This binding is never built as a GraalVM native image, so no GraalVM
# artifact is embedded - same pattern as the compression codecs above.
# Broadened to the full com.oracle.svm.* / org.graalvm.* namespace (not just
# the one sub-package that first surfaced) to avoid further one-at-a-time
# karaf-feature-verification failures for GraalVM-only support code.
#
# The following are all optional integrations documented directly in the
# netty-handler/netty-common/netty-buffer 4.2.10.Final POMs (verified against
# Maven Central, not guessed) that this binding never uses, since standard
# JDK TLS and SLF4J logging are sufficient:
#   - io.netty.internal.tcnative     -> optional OpenSSL-native TLS engine
#   - org.bouncycastle.jsse          -> optional BouncyCastle TLS engine
#                                        (netty-handler loads it via
#                                        Class.forName reflection)
#   - org.conscrypt                  -> optional Google Conscrypt TLS provider
#   - sun.misc / sun.nio.ch / jdk.jfr -> JDK-internal, netty-common's own
#                                        (Felix-based) manifest already marks
#                                        these optional; replicated here since
#                                        we regenerate the manifest ourselves
#   - sun.security.ssl / sun.security.x509 -> JDK-internal, referenced by
#                                        Netty's optional ALPN/SelfSignedCertificate
#                                        support code (netty-handler's own POM
#                                        notes needing --add-exports for
#                                        sun.security.x509 for this reason)
#   - org.apache.commons.logging     -> optional Netty logging backend
#   - org.apache.logging.log4j.*     -> optional Netty logging backend
#   - reactor.blockhound             -> optional BlockHound test integration
# org.openhab.core / org.openhab.core.*: without these two lines, bnd falls
# back to its own default versioning heuristic and stamps every
# org.openhab.core.* import with a strict version range derived from the
# exact core build we compile against (e.g. "[5.3,6)"), which then refuses
# to resolve against any other openHAB 5.x minor release (confirmed by
# diffing this bundle's generated MANIFEST.MF against
# org.openhab.binding.mercedesme's, a binding with no local bnd.bnd: its
# org.openhab.core.* imports carry NO version attribute at all, while every
# other provided package - Gson, javax.measure, Jetty, SLF4J - does get a
# normal range). Both a literal "org.openhab.core" entry AND a wildcard
# "org.openhab.core.*" entry are required - the wildcard alone does not
# match the bare root package. Both need the explicit ";version=!"
# attribute (bnd's syntax for "strip/suppress this attribute, never
# auto-fill it") - just omitting a ";version=" clause is NOT enough to stop
# bnd from computing one anyway; this was verified the hard way across
# three separate failed attempts before landing on ";version=!".
#
# NOTE: this pair of lines has already gone missing from this file once
# outside of a reviewed edit (replaced with a plain, version-less
# "org.openhab.core.*" entry that silently did not fix the resolution
# failure). If this file is hand-edited again, keep both lines with
# ";version=!" intact, or the exact "org.openhab.core; version=[5.3.0,6.0.0)"
# runtime failure will return.
# javax.jmdns / javax.jmdns.*: as of the 2026-08-01 correction, jmdns is no
# longer embedded (see pom.xml's dep.noembedding). This binding's own
# EEBusMdnsDiscoveryParticipant implements openHAB core's
# org.openhab.core.config.discovery.mdns.MDNSDiscoveryParticipant SPI, whose
# method signatures carry javax.jmdns.ServiceInfo from whatever jmDNS copy
# openHAB core itself provides at runtime. Embedding a second, private copy
# here made the JVM load two distinct classes both named
# javax.jmdns.ServiceInfo - a loader constraint violation (LinkageError:
# "activate cannot be found") at component activation, not a build-time
# failure, so it was not caught by karaf-feature-verification. Same
# ";version=!" treatment as org.openhab.core.* above and for the same
# reason: import whatever version core actually provides, not a strict
# range pinned to this bundle's own (now nonexistent, since unembedded)
# compile-time jmdns jar.
# Netty-common shades/relocates org.jctools to
# io.netty.util.internal.shaded.org.jctools.* at its own build time and
# stamps OSGi @Version package-info annotations onto the relocated
# packages. Once embedded here, bnd picks those annotations up and
# auto-exports the package (and separately imports it too) - the only
# embedded package that does this, since it is the only one carrying such
# annotations. This violates the "nothing embedded is exported" intent
# (see the Consequences/Positive section above) and was only found by
# diffing this bundle's manifest against org.openhab.binding.mercedesme's.
# Force it fully private: excluded from Export-Package, and excluded from
# Import-Package so bnd does not try to wire it externally either - we
# always use our own embedded copy.
#
# Bundle-SymbolicName: the presence of this bnd.bnd file makes bnd-maven-plugin ignore the
# <configuration><bnd>...</bnd></configuration> instructions inherited from the reactor POM
# entirely (confirmed live: `mvn help:effective-pom` correctly shows
# "Bundle-SymbolicName: org.openhab.binding.eebus" in the inherited plugin config, but the
# actual built jar's MANIFEST.MF had "Bundle-SymbolicName: org.openhab.addons.reactor.bundles"
# instead - bnd's own fallback default once this file's mere existence overrides the POM
# config). Set it explicitly here so it actually takes effect.
Bundle-SymbolicName: org.openhab.binding.eebus

# Export-Package is intentionally "export nothing" (bare "!*"), matching the
# ADR's Consequences/Positive statement that nothing embedded is exported. A
# trailing bare "*" here (i.e. "export everything bnd can see") previously
# caused bnd to sweep in unrelated content from elsewhere on its scan path -
# surfaced as "Invalid package name: 'repository.org.apache.felix...'" /
# 'resources.system...'" warnings for Karaf distro paths, and as a hard
# failure ("Same component name org.openhab.addons used in multiple
# component implementations") from two unrelated openHAB core SCR
# components getting swept into this bundle's component analysis. The
# explicit jctools exclusion is redundant once nothing is exported, but is
# kept for documentation of intent.
Export-Package: !io.netty.util.internal.shaded.org.jctools.*, !*
Import-Package: \
    !io.netty.util.internal.shaded.org.jctools.*, \
    org.openhab.core;version=!, \
    org.openhab.core.*;version=!, \
    javax.jmdns;version=!, \
    javax.jmdns.*;version=!, \
    com.aayushatharva.brotli4j.*;resolution:=optional, \
    com.github.luben.zstd.*;resolution:=optional, \
    net.jpountz.*;resolution:=optional, \
    lzma.sdk.*;resolution:=optional, \
    com.jcraft.jzlib.*;resolution:=optional, \
    com.ning.compress.*;resolution:=optional, \
    com.oracle.svm.*;resolution:=optional, \
    org.graalvm.*;resolution:=optional, \
    io.netty.internal.tcnative.*;resolution:=optional, \
    org.bouncycastle.jsse.*;resolution:=optional, \
    org.conscrypt.*;resolution:=optional, \
    sun.misc;resolution:=optional, \
    sun.nio.ch;resolution:=optional, \
    sun.security.ssl;resolution:=optional, \
    sun.security.x509;resolution:=optional, \
    jdk.jfr;resolution:=optional, \
    org.apache.commons.logging.*;resolution:=optional, \
    org.apache.logging.log4j.*;resolution:=optional, \
    reactor.blockhound.*;resolution:=optional, \
    io.netty.pkitesting.*;resolution:=optional, \
    *
